jobs.description:
Our client is a well-established Belgian group with a strong international footprint, operating in the services and insurance environment.

Jobomschrijving

Reporting to the Accounting Manager, you will take end-to-end ownership of the Group's consolidation activities, covering both Belgian GAAP and IFRS scopes.Your main responsibilities will include:

• Managing the end-to-end consolidation process across Belgian and international entities, covering both Belgian GAAP and IFRS reporting;
• Performing key consolidation operations, including intercompany eliminations, IFRS adjustments and foreign currency conversions;
• Preparing reliable consolidated financial reporting and coordinating the different closing cycles;
• Taking ownership of two consolidation scopes, including international entities and an IFRS scope mainly linked to insurance and real estate activities;
• Harmonizing accounting practices and ensuring consistency and quality of financial information across entities;
• Working closely with Accounting, Controlling, Tax, Treasury, M&A and external auditors;
• Improving consolidation tools, processes, reporting and internal controls;
• Building and further developing the consolidation function, with the ambition to move towards more frequent consolidation cycles.

• Master's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics or a related field;
• Around 5 to 7 years of relevant experience, with hands-on, end-to-end consolidation experience;
• Strong knowledge of Belgian GAAP and consolidation principles, with IFRS experience highly valued;
• Previous exposure to the insurance sector would be a strong asset;
• Comfortable working with Excel and consolidation/ERP tools;
• Good command of French, Dutch and English;
• Hands-on, autonomous and proactive, with the ability to thrive in an environment where processes are still evolving;
• Ambitious and eager to take ownership of a function and contribute to its future development.

For our client, a well-known company in the BRUGES region, we are looking for a RENOVATION WORKER.

Do you enjoy variety in your job and do you like renovation work? Then you are the person we are looking for!

As a RENOVATION WORKER in the BRUGES region, your day will look like this:

• Together with your colleagues, you will carry out demolition and repair work as part of renovation projects;
• Carrying out general renovation works on houses and buildings;
• Demolition works and preparing the construction site;
• Bricklaying, plastering and small concrete works;
• Installing and repairing floors and walls;
• Installing insulation and drywall/plasterboard;
• Ensuring that the entire renovation project is completed to a high standard;
• Ensuring that structural works and stability requirements are properly taken into account.
As a RENOVATION WORKER in BRUGES, you have the following qualities:

• You have solid work experience as a renovation worker and are fully familiar with flooring, carpentry, bricklaying, etc.;
• You have a category B driving licence;
• The starting location is Bruges (Blauwe-Toren), at the company’s warehouse;
• You speak Dutch or English;
• You are not afraid of heights.

We are looking for a Business Process Engineer for our customer in Kortenberg

Main tasks and responsibilities:

This role fits in the implementation and introduction of a new ERP and other systms for providing services to our customers. Togetherwith the European team, you will be analyzing the existing processes and defining the best practices and contribute to a succesfull roll-out and maintenance of the new ERP system and other systems.

Investigating and Analyzing current business processes, procedures and requirements and mapping them to SharePoint;
Documenting visualization of process and procedure flows;
Identification and assessment of potential risks in business processes and development of risk mitigation strategies;
Re-engineering and optimization of business processes and shaping new process policies;
Proposing smarter process management solutions for performance improvement and cost reduction;
Illustrating project descriptions, objectives, and measurements;
Collaboration with various stakeholders to identify potential for improvement;
Participate in and hold meetings to perform incremental agile software development framework when managing product development;
Support to evaluate and test administrative system changes to provide ongoing support to existing applications and implement new applications;
Staying updated with new software features and industry trends and educating people in the group.
Profile:
Several years of experience in business process analysis and optimization;
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;
Ability to critically question processes;
Excellent communication and teamwork skills;
Accuracy and care in the analysis and documentation of processes;
Language skills in English mandatory.

Professional skills:
Excellent knowledge of Business Process Modeling, Business Process Reengineering and the related Management (BPM) Tools;
SharePoint: Knowledge in using SharePoint for mapping business requirements and managing document workflows;
Data Analysis Tools: Skills in using tools like Excel or Power BI for analyzing business data and visualizing process flows;

Nice to have:

Knowledge in SAP S/4HANA public cloud;
Agile Frameworks: Understanding and applying agile methodologies for software development and project management;
Software Testing: Experience in professional software testing and quality assurance;
Experience in Project Management and related Software is an advantage: Experience with tools like JIRA, Trello, or Microsoft Project for managing tasks and tracking progress;
Programming Languages: A basic understanding of programming languages like Python, Java, or C# can be advantageous for accurately assessing the feasibility of proposed changes.
